	(text "SAE Formula EV\nLow-Voltage Wiring Overview"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 342.9 24.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.81 3.81)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ed1e6d4e-284f-46b8-aace-1634799b0542")
	)
	(text_box "PCBs are contained within Cinch 5810130065 4\" x 3.35\" enclosures and\nutilize Cinch 5810132011 32 position PCB header.\n\nThis header has a 20-Pin and a 12-Pin Molex male plugs\n\nThe correct Molex MX150 female harness plugs to attach to the enclosure are:\n\n334721206 or 334721201 (Black, 12-pin, keying option A)\n\n334722007 or 334722002 (Gray, 20-pin, keying option B)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.392 187.2789 0)
		(size 120.65 50.9731)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b04a168d-c920-4668-8495-2a214355ee09")
	)
	(text_box "yellow = CAN High\ngreen = CAN Low\nred = LV Power (12-36 V)\nblack = LV Ground\n\nModules are powered via the main Low-Voltage bus (red and black) and communicate\nwith each other with CAN via the main CAN bus (green and yellow)\n\nEach module sheet contains the wiring and components specific to that circuit along with the part numbers for connectors.\n\nTo add a new module:\n1.) Create a new hierarchical sheet (or copy an existing one) and label it appropriately \n2.) Implement module specific components and connections within sheet\n3.) Place VDD, GND, CANH, and CANL sheet pins and connect to main bus\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 292.1 31.75 0)
		(size 107.95 114.2999)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
